            <ArticleTitle>Pelviureteric junction obstruction and recurrent abdominal pain in childhood.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>818-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three cases of recurrent abdominal pain due to pelviureteric junction obstruction in childhood are presented. Ultrasound is useful in confirming the diagnosis and pyeloplasty is recommended.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
